 Yucatán Peninsula, south of both Florida and the Bahamas, west of Hispaniola, and north of Jamaica and the Cayman Islands. Cuba is the largest country in the Caribbean by area and the third-largest by population, after Haiti and the Dominican Republic. Culturally, Cuba is considered to be part of Latin America. Its capital and largest city is Havana.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"CU"}],"arc":{"reports":3,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T22:34:48Z","first_title":"National Atomic Testing Museum to Host “Atomic Stories” Event Examining Cuban Missile Crisis, Saturday, Oct. 24","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"Nevada Business Magazine","earlier":[{"id":"e_c5644b854024","title":"National Atomic Testing Museum to Host “Atomic Stories” Event Examining Cuban Missile Crisis, Saturday, Oct. 24","date":"2026-10-12T22:34:48Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"Nevada Business Magazine","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_169dc9aa2a90","title":"Richard Heyser’s U-2 Flight That Started the Cuban Missile Crisis","date":"2026-10-13T10:18:45Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipAFBVV95cUxNN183Sk1IbVkyU0l5VVY2bWVraTZxZ3pvQnFxN0dvNmdaeGVQakZjcVZuRkxsdlkwTG9LS0FNUFBXOWx5Z2s1TTd3RlNGRUpGYy1sMXBNd25nclRiZTJFZEFCWnZQRFZNeWdDNUJ1d2oyQmx5LXFRdkJHZEwyanc0Ynk2RXRWTTJmVUozZVZVOVprY0tKRlZEYjJlWVVKbVlNcEdJMA?oc=5","publisher":"MiGFlug","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_123df84acf02","title":"JFK Learns That Soviet Missiles Are in Cuba—The Cuban Missile Crisis, Day One","date":"2026-10-16T15:07:16Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQTldRZWs0OW1GanU3ZmRxaTM5VExKR1RKSWxYZlRjaHNRa2dvbFNRNHRtMUF4N2cxcFFncF9LT3RacU1OM1RjaEdUelBrMjJhSDBxV1NlYzF2ZE9XUGg2MjNCcHlRWlNncFktNlNfYjZiWmFYMWlvOGYwbjd3NFdTX1B3T0NjVS1JdVE3MWZoSFZsUTJqOU1TRWRGVzZwYmhUTzFZZ3ZSYzQ?oc=5","publisher":"Council on Foreign Relations","verification":"single_source_report"}],"we